Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Toffee Mixture</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">unsalted butter</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">brown sugar</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">graham cracker crumbs</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Toppings</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">semisweet chocolate chips</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">chopped pecans</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">pinch</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-5317-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5317\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 8×8-inch baking pan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">Line with parchment paper for easy removal.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Saucepan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For melting butter and sugar.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-5317-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-5317-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5317\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C). This will ensure your Toffee Bars bake evenly and perfectly.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Line an 8×8-inch baking pan with parchment paper. This makes it easy to lift out the bars later.</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Making the Toffee</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-1-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a saucepan over medium heat, melt butter and brown sugar. Stir constantly until the mixture is smooth and bubbly.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-1-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Remove the saucepan from heat and stir in salt. Spread the toffee mixture evenly over the graham cracker crumbs in the pan.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-1-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Bake in the preheated oven for 10–12 minutes until bubbly. Keep an eye on it to avoid burning!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-1-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Remove from the oven and immediately sprinkle chocolate chips over the hot toffee layer. Let sit for 2 minutes to melt.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-1-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Once melted, spread the chocolate evenly over the toffee layer. This is where the magic happens!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-1-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Sprinkle chopped pecans on top of the melted chocolate for that extra crunch and flavor.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5317-step-1-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Cool completely in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour. Once set, lift out of the pan and cut into bars. Enjoy your sweet success!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-5317-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>28g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients-for-toffee-bars\"><strong>Ingredients for Toffee Bars</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these delicious ingredients to create the best Toffee Bars!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ingredients-for-Toffee-Bars.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for Toffee Bars displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-5315\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ingredients-for-Toffee-Bars.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Ingredients-for-Toffee-Bars-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – unsalted butter</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – brown sugar</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cups</strong> – graham cracker crumbs</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – semisweet chocolate chips</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ cup</strong> – chopped pecans (optional)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>pinch</strong> – salt</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-toffee-bars\"><strong>How to Make Toffee Bars</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up some delicious <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toffee\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Toffee </a>Bars! The preparation time is about 15 minutes, cooking time is 10–12 minutes, and you&#8217;ll want to let them cool in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour before cutting. Let&#8217;s dive in!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Making-Toffee-Bars.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making Toffee Bars, including preheating the oven, preparing the baking pan, melting butter and brown sugar, and spreading the toffee mixture.\" class=\"wp-image-5316\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Making-Toffee-Bars.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Making-Toffee-Bars-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C). This will ensure your Toffee Bars bake evenly and perfectly.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Prepare the Baking Pan</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Line an 8×8-inch baking pan with parchment paper. This makes it easy to lift out the bars later.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Make the Toffee Mixture</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a saucepan over medium heat, melt butter and brown sugar. Stir constantly until the mixture is smooth and bubbly.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Add Salt and Spread</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the saucepan from heat and stir in salt. Spread the toffee mixture evenly over the graham cracker crumbs in the pan.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Bake the Toffee Layer</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bake in the preheated oven for 10–12 minutes until bubbly. Keep an eye on it to avoid burning!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Add Chocolate Chips</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove from the oven and immediately sprinkle chocolate chips over the hot toffee layer. Let sit for 2 minutes to melt.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Spread the Chocolate</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once melted, spread the chocolate evenly over the toffee layer. This is where the magic happens!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Add Pecans</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sprinkle chopped pecans on top of the melted chocolate for that extra crunch and flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 9: Cool and Cut</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cool completely in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour. Once set, lift out of the pan and cut into bars. Enjoy your sweet success!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Dessert</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>12 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>60 minutes (Resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>87 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Chilled and cut into bars!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-toffee-bars\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Toffee Bars</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use high-quality chocolate for a richer flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chill the bars before cutting for cleaner edges.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with nuts for added crunch and flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Keep an eye on the baking time to avoid overcooking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in an airtight container to maintain freshness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-toffee-bars\"><strong>How to Serve this Toffee Bars</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve warm with a scoop of vanilla ice cream on top.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a drizzle of chocolate sauce for extra indulgence.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a cup of hot cocoa or coffee for a cozy treat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with chopped nuts for added crunch and flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cut into bite-sized pieces for a perfect party snack.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in colorful cellophane for a delightful homemade gift.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Toffee Bars can be made ahead and stored for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Toffee Bars Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow Toffee Bars to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in an airtight container at room temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Keep away from direct sunlight and heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Consume within 5-7 days for best freshness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Toffee Bars</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap Toffee Bars tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped bars in a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 3 months for optimal quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Toffee Bars</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw frozen Toffee Bars in the refrigerator overnight.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For a warm treat, microwave for 10-15 seconds.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, reheat in a preheated oven at 350°F for 5-7 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy warm for the best texture and taste!</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is the name of the toffee candy bar?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The name of the popular toffee candy bar is often referred to as a &#8216;Toffee Bar.&#8217; However, there are specific brands like &#8216;Skor&#8217; and &#8216;Heath&#8217; that are well-known for their toffee-filled chocolate bars. These bars typically feature a crunchy toffee center coated in rich chocolate, making them a delightful treat for toffee lovers!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Should toffee bars be refrigerated?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Toffee bars do not necessarily need to be refrigerated, but storing them in a cool, dry place can help maintain their texture and flavor. If you live in a warm climate, refrigerating them can prevent the chocolate from melting. Just be sure to let them come to room temperature before enjoying for the best taste!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What can I make with toffee?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Toffee can be used in a variety of delicious recipes! You can incorporate it into cookies, brownies, or even ice cream for a delightful crunch. Additionally, toffee can be used as a topping for cakes or mixed into trail mixes for a sweet and salty snack. The possibilities are endless!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Are Skor bars toffee?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, Skor bars are indeed toffee! They consist of a crunchy toffee center coated in rich milk chocolate. This combination makes them a favorite among toffee enthusiasts. If you love the taste of toffee, Skor bars are a perfect treat to satisfy your cravings!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There you have it—your very own batch of delightful Toffee Bars! These sweet treats are not just easy to make, but they also bring a wave of nostalgia with every bite. So gather your loved ones, whip up this simple recipe, and enjoy the rewarding taste of homemade goodness. Happy baking!</p>\n",
